Chapter 7: Implementation Design as a Mathematical Specification

No empirical experiments are performed; this chapter provides a precise algorithmic blueprint suitable for translation into code.

7.1 Data Structures

Capsule: c = (\text{id},\; \mathbf{W}_c \in \mathbb{R}^{d\times n},\; \mathbf{u}_c \in \mathbb{R}^d,\; \mu_c,\; \sigma_c,\; \nu_c,\; H_c,\; \mathbf{g}_c \in \mathbb{R}^G,\; \text{nucleus\_id}), with all statistics updated via EWMA with time constant \tau_\text{stat}.

Highway: h = (\text{id},\; \text{src},\; \text{dst},\; \mathbf{W}^\text{fast},\; \mathbf{W}^\text{slow},\; \alpha,\; \nu).

Nucleus: n = (\text{id},\; \mathcal{C},\; \boldsymbol{\theta}) where \boldsymbol{\theta} = (\theta_\sigma,\; \theta_\nu,\; \theta_H,\; \lambda,\; N_\max,\; \kappa,\; \beta,\; T_\text{quorum},\; \eta_O,\; \lambda_O,\; \dots).

Gene-expression state: \Gamma = (\mathbf{O} \in \mathbb{R}^{G\times G},\; \eta_O,\; \lambda_O).

Global state: \Sigma = (\mathcal{N},\; \mathcal{C}_\text{all},\; \mathcal{H}_\text{all},\; \Gamma,\; \mathbf{x},\; T,\; \text{event\_log}).

7.2 Core Algorithms

Algorithm 7.1 (Forward Pass with Adaptive Routing).

1. For each capsule i: \mathbf{u}_i = \tilde{f}(\mathbf{W}_i\mathbf{x}_\text{input}).
2. For each highway (i,j): \hat{\mathbf{u}}_{j|i} = \mathbf{W}_{ij}^\text{eff}\mathbf{u}_i.
3. Initialise b_{ij} = 0. Repeat until \|\mathbf{c}^{(t)} - \mathbf{c}^{(t-1)}\|_1 < \varepsilon_r or t = T_\max:
   · c_{ij} = \text{softmax}_j(b_{ij})
   · \mathbf{s}_j = \sum_i c_{ij}\hat{\mathbf{u}}_{j|i}, \mathbf{v}_j = \tilde{f}(\mathbf{s}_j)
   · b_{ij} \leftarrow b_{ij} + \mathbf{v}_j\cdot\hat{\mathbf{u}}_{j|i}
4. Output \mathbf{v}_j as capsule activations; update rolling statistics.

Algorithm 7.2 (Plasticity Update).
For each highway (i,j), compute \Delta\mathbf{W}_{ij}^\text{fast} according to the chosen plasticity rule. Apply homeostatic scaling: compute E_j, scaling factor \alpha = T/(E_j + \varepsilon_0); if \|\mathbf{v}_j\| > 1-\zeta, scale down and apply barrier penalty. Update \mathbf{O} via: \mathbf{O} \leftarrow \text{sym}\!\left(\mathbf{O} + \eta_O\sum_{(i,j)}(B_{ij}-p_{ij})\mathbf{g}_i\mathbf{g}_j^\top - \eta_O\lambda_O\mathbf{O}\right) where sym(\cdot) symmetrises.

Algorithm 7.3 (Consensus-Based Generation).

1. Each capsule computes \psi_c via the hybrid trigger.
2. Broadcast (\psi_c, \mathbf{m}_c) to neighbours within cluster distance (gossip, O(\log N) rounds).
3. If quorum q reached: collect anomaly buffer, run Algorithm 3.4 (meta-expansion), create new capsule(s) with gene-regulated connectivity from Definition 4.2. Log event with timestamp.

Algorithm 7.4 (Consolidation).
Update \alpha_c = \sigma(\kappa(\theta_\text{cons} - \sigma_c)). For each incoming highway: \mathbf{W}^\text{slow} \leftarrow \mathbf{W}^\text{slow} + \eta_\text{cons}(1-\alpha_c)(\mathbf{W}^\text{fast} - \mathbf{W}^\text{slow}).

Algorithm 7.5 (Causal Emergence Computation).

1. Collect trajectory \{\mathbf{q}(t)\}_{t=1}^N.
2. Apply PCA to project to \mathbf{z}_t \in \mathbb{R}^{d_\text{proj}}.
3. Estimate \widehat{\text{CP}}_c via k-NN KL estimator on \{(\mathbf{z}_t, \mathbf{z}_{t+1})\}.
4. For each coarse-graining \phi in a set of random coarse-grainings, compute macro-kernel K^\phi and \text{CP}_\text{macro}^\phi.
5. Compute U_k, D_k for each scale, normalise (Lemma 6.1), compute \bar{\mathcal{E}}, compute \tilde{\mathcal{D}} (Definition 6.5).

7.3 Persistence: Event-Sourced Logging

Structural events and significant weight changes are logged with a surprise-based threshold: log if |x - \mu_x|/(\sigma_x + \varepsilon) > \tau_\text{surprise} or with probability p_\text{sample} regardless.

Theorem 7.1 (Logging Completeness). Under the assumption that logged quantities have approximately Gaussian marginals with finite variance, the expected fraction of true statistical outliers (3-\sigma events) captured is at least 1 - \Phi(\tau_\text{surprise}) + p_\text{sample}\Phi(\tau_\text{surprise}), where \Phi is the standard normal CDF.

